      "message": "feat(motion): engagement-controlled trochoidal slot generator\n\nTrochoid loops (Otkur & Lazoglu 2007; Rauch, Duc & Hascoet 2009) laid\nalong a centre chain: each loop is the front arc of a circle that meets\nthe band's walls at 10 degrees, so the arcs of a straight chain are\ntranslates and never cross (the verifier's crossing law); a wall lead\ncuts the cusp to the next loop, a helix bores the start and a pencil of\narcs closes the far cap. The returns are microlift retraces of the arc\njust cut (or retract hops).\n\nThe engagement is measured, not assumed: each candidate step (a ladder\ndown from the user's) is walked on quality's dexel yardstick, first on\nits first 12 loops, then on the whole level, and the first step under\nthe limit is kept (said in a note). Refused by name: a channel too\nnarrow for the tool, a loop band wider than the room, a limit no step\nholds, a loop leaving the channel, a crossing, and a lifted return that\nwould stand over stock (lifted_cut reads inside the cutter's disc on the\nin-process stock).\n\nPins: the full-width slot reads 66.5 deg against the straight slot's\n180; a 60 deg limit cuts the step; verifier clean (no crossing, gouge or\nrapid in stock) climb/conventional x microlift/retract; returns on air.\n\nRefs #220\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
